'''Li'l Bun Bun''' (ちびぶんぶん, '''''Chibi Bun Bun''''') is a [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy that appears in [[Legend Stages]]. He was added in [[Version 5.4 Update|Version 5.4]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Li'l Bun Bun
|image = E 272.png
|first appearance = '''SoL''': [[Trouble at the Mansion|Sub-chapter 32 - Trouble at the Mansion]]
|money drop = 300¢ - 1,185¢
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Putrid Prison|Sub-chapter 13 - Putrid Prison]]
}}

==Enemy==
[[Teacher Bun Bun]]'s son has fast movement and attacks, fairly high health and attack power, and, perhaps most importantly, drops a minuscule amount of cash when dying. However, he still has many knockbacks and shorter range. He is known for being sent out in hordes and/or spawned infinitely like a very strong peon. With their high movement speed and rapid attacks, Li'l Bun Buns quickly meet up with each other to form a stack, doing insane DPS to whatever they touch.

In most of his appearances, he is buffed to at least 1,000%, giving him about 0.75x as much health but 1.25x as much attack power as the 400% Teacher Bun Bun from the [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon/Iriomote]].

==Strategy==
Treat him like a pure Floating [[Shy Boy]] with more damage and slower attacks, but devise a cost-efficient way to get rid of him as he drops much less cash. He can be beaten easily by [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|Anti-Floating Units]] that do high damage like [[Archer Cat (Rare Cat)|Cataur]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], or cats with high area damage, such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] or [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]]. His low range sometimes provides an opportunity to use rushers like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]].

